- `process initiation`: Omits the explicitly documented step `"begin by checking if the order has been received"` before proceeding to sum evaluation. (SMC1)
- `action(n7, "end")`: Hallucinates a discrete task; the source only states `"the process will come to an end"` immediately after bill creation, which corresponds to `end(e1)`, not a separate action. (SMC1, SMC2)
- `action(n6, "continue process and create bill")`: Conflates two sequentially distinct phases—`"continue with the process"` (triggered when sum < 500) and `"Finally, create the bill"`—violating the chronological progression described in the text. (SMC2, SMC3)
- `defines(v1, "check sum of order", {">2000", "1000-1500", "500-999", "<500"})`: Encodes numeric thresholds as a finite set of string literals instead of numeric interval ranges, failing to faithfully reflect the quantitative comparisons like `"falls between 1000 and 1500"` and `"greater than 2000"`. (SMC6)

